==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_AccessControl  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_AccessControl.als
    rationale: Clearing the access-control fact lets the model invent a Permitted operation whose (role, kind) pair is not in the policy matrix — e.g., a hospital_administrator reading a clinical record — which is exactly what LeastPrivilege, FR_005, and FR_017 are meant to catch.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, FR_005_AdminNoClinicalContent, FR_017_AdminOnlyAudit, OwnershipBasedAccess, FR_004_CareTeamGating
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_005_AdminNoClinicalContent: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_017_AdminOnlyAudit: FAIL (expected)
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_004_CareTeamGating: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_NotesAppendOnly  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_NotesAppendOnly.als
    rationale: Clearing the no-NoteEdit fact lets the model invent a clinical-note mutation event, which the append-only invariant exists to forbid.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_011_NotesAppendOnly
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_011_NotesAppendOnly: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditAppendOnly  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_AuditAppendOnly.als
    rationale: Clearing the no-AuditMutation fact lets the model invent an audit-entry mutation, violating immutability (FR-014) and the 7-year retention floor (FR-016).
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_014_AuditImmutable, FR_016_AuditRetention
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_014_AuditImmutable: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_016_AuditRetention: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditCompleteness  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_AuditCompleteness.als
    rationale: Clearing audit completeness lets a Read/AddNote operation occur with no audit entry, violating the always-on-audit invariant and the SLA-enforced rollback rule.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_012_AlwaysOnAudit, FR_015_AuditSLA
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_012_AlwaysOnAudit: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_015_AuditSLA: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_Attribution  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_Attribution.als
    rationale: Clearing attribution lets an audit entry record an accessor different from the actual operation caller, violating audit-entry correctness.
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectness, FR_013_AuditFields
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_013_AuditFields: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_NonPermittedResponseIs404  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_NonPermittedResponseIs404.als
    rationale: Clearing the byte-equivalent-404 invariant lets a denied operation return a clinical-content response, distinguishing denial from not-found and leaking patient existence.
    expected to FAIL: NoInformationLeakage, FR_006_ByteEquivalentDenied
      - NoInformationLeakage: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_006_ByteEquivalentDenied: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AdminResponseNoClinicalContent  → runs/C-L2/mutated_F_AdminResponseNoClinicalContent.als
    rationale: Clearing admin content-blindness lets a ListAudit response carry a clinical-read shape, exactly the FR-018 forbidden case.
    expected to FAIL: FR_018_AdminContentBlind, FR_005_AdminNoClinicalContent
      - FR_018_AdminContentBlind: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_005_AdminNoClinicalContent: FAIL (expected)

